<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/rota/requests">Shift Requests</a> lists everything waiting for you at the location,
        in three groups.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Can't make it">
        <FluentText>
            Someone has said they can't work a shift. <strong>Let them off</strong> makes the shift open, and
            everyone who could work it is told. <strong>Keep them on</strong> leaves them on it. Call-offs always
            come to a manager.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Open shifts asked for">
        <FluentText>
            Each open shift shows who has asked for it. Select <strong>Give it to them</strong> for one person,
            or <strong>No</strong> to turn a request down.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Swaps agreed">
        <FluentText>
            Two people have agreed to swap shifts. Select <strong>Approve swap</strong> or <strong>Turn down</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Do pick-ups and swaps need you?">
        <FluentText>
            The <strong>Pick-ups and swaps need a manager's approval</strong> switch at the top decides this
            for the location.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>On</strong>: staff ask for open shifts and agree swaps, and you decide here.</li>
            <li><strong>Off</strong>: the first person to pick up an open shift gets it, and swaps happen as soon as
                both people agree.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            To offer a shift yourself, open it on the Rota Builder and choose <strong>Open up for cover</strong>.
            If a request can't be decided, for example because the person is missing required training, the
            card says why.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
